        "original_id": "ab02e00f-4550-5993-a15b-ead092a111bd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Basil LeFlore\n- Places: Carrollton, Mississippi; Goodland, Indian Territory; Indian Territory\n- Organizations: Choctaw Nation; United States Government\n- Roles: Governor\n- Concepts: Indian Territory; Indian country; Native American relocation; aboriginal title\n\nFacts:\n- Basil LeFlore was born near Carrollton, Mississippi, in 1811.\n- Indian Territory, the Indian Territories, and Indian country were general terms for an evolving land area set aside by the United States Government for relocating Native Americans who held aboriginal title to their land.\n- Basil LeFlore was governor of the Choctaw Nation after the Choctaw removal to Indian Territory.\n- Basil LeFlore died in Goodland, Indian Territory, on 15 October 1886.",
